  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/8c4b58c0e0508fbea7df9619b8086fd70d1a367df36e31d0d7b9ecc7eb0f4378.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, compress it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $0.5$ to give $y=-0.5cos\u2061x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-0.5cos\u2061x.$",
